      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHO'S BENT (1) will be peaking third up from a spell, and he is dropping down in class from his last run. A good draw, and a 3kg claim makes him the one to beat in the small field. SPINARELLA (4) capped off some good form with a well-timed run to score by a short head at Belmont just over 5 weeks ago in a tougher field than she meets here. She only rises half a kilo in weight, and she can repeat the dose. SOMETHING ROYAL (3) was a touch disappointing when finishing fifth here 18 days ago as the favourite. She is normally very consistent, and will have the aid of a 4kg claim this time. Stick with her. Each way. MANTUA (6) has not won for some time, and his last run was only plain. He drops further down in weight and is worth another chance in the small field. GREAT PROMISE (2) was ridden off the pace last time out and finished third, continuing her terrific run of minor placings this prep. She can secure a soft run from the pole position and should be fighting out the finish.",
